WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.590 align:start position:0%
 
just moments  after andre hill walked out of a garage  at a house where he was a guest  he was shot by police put your  hands out to the side hands out to the  side now  roll to your stomach now body cam  footage from officers in columbus ohio  appears to show andre hill an unarmed  black man  still alive as he lay wounded on the  ground  for more than five minutes officers left  him lying there without giving  any first aid mr hill was wearing a  black lives matter t-shirt under his  sweater  calling for justice for george floyd  [Music]  it then took between 5 and 13 minutes  before  anyone attempted to save andre hill's  life  according to his family's lawyer  everybody turn your cameras on camera's  on for the residents  anybody doing anything for them sir we  contact  medics  get some gloves you got gloves up yes  sir start pumping his chest  it was too late for the 47 year old who  became yet another unarmed black man  to die in an encounter with law  enforcement in america  where is the humanity for andre hill  where is the humanity  this columbus citizen  police officers were responding to a  non-emergency call from a neighbor  over a noise complaint when they  encountered mr hill  the white officer who fired the shots  adam coy  has now been sacked another officer  who was with him that night told an  internal police interview  she didn't feel andre hill posed a  danger did you observe any threats from  the subject  no were any verbal warnings given by  officer coy  no we had the expectation that he was  going to come out and talk to us  the conduct of all police staff who were  there on the 22nd of december is now  being investigated  andre hill should be alive today a  columbus police officer  is responsible for his death i can't  defend it  i can't make it right but i will do what  is in my power  andre hill's daughter is haunted  imagining her father  in his final moments i got to memorize  my dad on the floor for the rest of my  life and how nobody helped him how  there's 22 officers on the scene with  body footage and not  one of them helped my dad the family  says they won't stop  until they have justice for andre hill  sally lockwood sky news new york

